.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH bhtune-simulate 1  "bhtune-simulate " 
.SH NAME
bhtune\-simulate \- Run a zero\-configuration demo MRFT tune against the built\-in FOPDT simulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbhtune\-simulate\fR [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-tagname\fR] [\fB\-\-template\fR] [\fB\-\-process\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-controller\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-relay\-amp\fR] [\fB\-\-cycles\-skip\fR] [\fB\-\-cycles\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-noise\-protection\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-mrft\-delay\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-tau\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-dead\-time\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-noise\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-seed\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-initial\-pv\fR] [\fB\-\-sim\-initial\-mv\fR] [\fB\-\-poll\-interval\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-write\-pid\fR] [\fB\-\-op\-timeout\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-restore\-timeout\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a zero\-configuration demo MRFT tune against the built\-in FOPDT simulator
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tagname\fR \fI<TAGNAME>\fR [default: Sim.Loop1.PV]

.TP
\fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR [default: Yokogawa CentumVP]

.TP
\fB\-\-process\-type\fR \fI<PROCESS_TYPE>\fR [default: flow]

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
flow
.IP \(bu 2
pressure\-line
.IP \(bu 2
pressure\-vessel
.IP \(bu 2
level
.IP \(bu 2
temperature\-mixing
.IP \(bu 2
temperature\-heat\-exchange
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-controller\-type\fR \fI<CONTROLLER_TYPE>\fR [default: pi]

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
p
.IP \(bu 2
pi
.IP \(bu 2
pid
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-relay\-amp\fR \fI<RELAY_AMP>\fR [default: 10]

.TP
\fB\-\-cycles\-skip\fR \fI<CYCLES_SKIP>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-cycles\-count\fR \fI<CYCLES_COUNT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-noise\-protection\-secs\fR \fI<NOISE_PROTECTION_SECS>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-mrft\-delay\fR \fI<MRFT_DELAY>\fR [default: 0]

.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-gain\fR \fI<SIM_GAIN>\fR [default: 1]

.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-tau\fR \fI<SIM_TAU>\fR [default: 2]

.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-dead\-time\fR \fI<SIM_DEAD_TIME>\fR [default: 5]

.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-noise\fR \fI<SIM_NOISE>\fR [default: 0]

.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-seed\fR \fI<SIM_SEED>\fR [default: 0]

.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-initial\-pv\fR \fI<SIM_INITIAL_PV>\fR [default: 50]

.TP
\fB\-\-sim\-initial\-mv\fR \fI<SIM_INITIAL_MV>\fR [default: 50]

.TP
\fB\-\-poll\-interval\-ms\fR \fI<POLL_INTERVAL_MS>\fR [default: 800]

.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\-secs\fR \fI<TIMEOUT_SECS>\fR [default: 3600]
See `TuneArgs::timeout_secs`
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\fR \fI<NOTES>\fR
Operator notes to attach to this run. See [`TuneArgs::notes`]
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
See `TuneArgs::yes`
.TP
\fB\-\-write\-pid\fR \fI<WRITE_PID>\fR
See `TuneArgs::write_pid`. Note the built\-in FOPDT simulator has no PID constant tags at all (see `build_loop_tags`), so write\-back is always skipped for `simulate` regardless of this flag \-\- it\*(Aqs accepted here purely so `simulate`\*(Aqs flag surface stays a strict defaulted subset of `tune`\*(Aqs, matching every other field
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
aggressive
.IP \(bu 2
moderate
.IP \(bu 2
sluggish
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-op\-timeout\-secs\fR \fI<OP_TIMEOUT_SECS>\fR [default: 30]
See `TuneArgs::op_timeout_secs`
.TP
\fB\-\-restore\-timeout\-secs\fR \fI<RESTORE_TIMEOUT_SECS>\fR [default: 30]
See `TuneArgs::restore_timeout_secs`
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: table]
See `TuneArgs::output`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: Human\-readable text (default)
.IP \(bu 2
json: Pretty\-printed JSON. This is the external contract for scripted/scheduled consumers, so its shape must not change silently once shipped
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
